AIOps (Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations) uses machine learning (ML) and large language models (LLMs) to monitor, analyze, correlate, and 
automate IT operations tasks — like incident detection, root cause analysis (RCA), anomaly detection, and self-healing.

| Layer                             | Function                                  | Example Tools                                               |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
|  Data Collection**           | Collect metrics, logs, traces, and events | Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, ELK, New Relic, Cloud Logging    |
|  Data Storage & Processing** | Store and preprocess data streams         | BigQuery, ElasticSearch, InfluxDB, Kafka                    |
|  AI / ML Analytics**         | Detect anomalies, predict failures        | Python (Isolation Forest, LSTM), Vertex AI, OpenAI API      |
|  Correlation & Insights**    | Combine multiple signals into insights    | LangChain, Gemini 2.5 Flash, or Mistral                     |
|  Automation / Response**     | Execute remediation workflows             | Cloud Functions, Cloud Run, Jenkins, ServiceNow, Slack Bots |


AIOps (Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations) refers to the application of AI, ML, and data analytics to automate and enhance IT operations such as monitoring,
event correlation, anomaly detection, root cause analysis, and incident remediation.

It integrates observability (logs, metrics, traces) with intelligent analytics to provide proactive insights and automated responses — reducing downtime and improving reliability.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

[Node Exporter / App Logs] --> [Prometheus + Loki] --> [AI Anomaly Engine]
                               ↑                       ↓
                          [Promtail]          [AI Log Insights API]
                               ↓                       ↓
                        [Grafana AI Dashboard]  <---  [Alertmanager]


Data sources: VMs, Kubernetes nodes, applications.

AI modules: detect anomalies, compute severity scores, correlate events.

Visualization: Grafana shows real-time anomaly trends and RCA insights.
Example Use Case

Scenario: CPU usage spikes across multiple nodes at 3 AM.

Prometheus detects metric anomalies.

AI Anomaly Insights API computes anomaly score = 0.92.

Grafana Dashboard highlights anomaly and root cause (e.g., failed cron job).

Alertmanager triggers Cloud Function to restart impacted service.
Result → Outage prevented automatically.

Business Impact

 60–80% reduction in Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)
 40–60% faster Mean Time to Resolve (MTTR)
 Automated early detection of performance degradation
 Reduced alert noise through AI correlation
 Proactive capacity planning and predictive scaling

